    <string name="narrator_natural">Natural voices, on this phone</string>
    <string name="narrator_natural_help">Kokoro. The most lifelike of the free voices, and they work offline. One %1$d MB download for all of them. A slower phone may pause between sentences while it renders.</string>
    <string name="narrator_lite">Lite voices, on this phone</string>
    <string name="narrator_lite_only">Voices on this phone</string>
    <string name="narrator_lite_help">Piper. Free and offline, small downloads (%1$d to %2$d MB each) and fast on any phone, but they sound less natural.</string>
    <string name="narrator_system">The phone\'s own voice</string>
    <string name="narrator_system_help">Android\'s text-to-speech: nothing to download, and offline once the phone has the %1$s voice data. How it sounds depends on the phone; often robotic.</string>
    <string name="narrator_system_default">Default system voice</string>
    <string name="narrator_elevenlabs">ElevenLabs, with your own key</string>
    <string name="narrator_elevenlabs_help">Studio quality, and one voice speaks every story language. ElevenLabs charges credits per character, about 600 to 1,000 a story; a story heard again is free. Needs a connection, and the stories\' text is sent to ElevenLabs. Without a connection an on-device voice reads on.</string>
